          "path": "_m/q/w/8/5/singhasari-temple-wp/candi-singosari-java-1332.jpg",
          "filename": "Candi Singosari, Java 1332.jpg",
          "caption": "This temple has been proposed as the funerary temple of Singosari Kertanagara (ruled 1268 - 1292), the last king of the Singosari dynasty. The temple's unfinished state can be judged from the incomplete kala over its entrance. The temple faces west. Its lower level is Shaiva, but according to the Blue Guide (p. 80), the temple has a second cella, on the upper level, that was a Buddhist dedication.",
